msgid "Ahead-of-time (AOT) caching"
msgstr "事前コンパイル（AOT）キャッシュ"

msgid "Starting with JDK 24, link:https://openjdk.org/projects/leyden/[Project Leyden] introduces AOT caching capabilities that can dramatically reduce startup time while keeping the full JVM runtime."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus provides a specialized `aot-jar` packaging type and build integration for generating AOT caches.\n"
"Build an AOT-optimized application with:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Then run it with:"
msgstr ""

msgid "AOT caching is a good fit when:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Cold start matters but you are not ready to adopt native images."
msgstr ""

msgid "You want to keep full JVM tooling: debuggers, profilers, JFR, and JMX all work normally."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can run a training step as part of your build pipeline to generate the AOT cache."
msgstr ""

msgid "The trade-offs are:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Larger deployment artifact. The AOT cache file adds approximately 40 MB for a small application, and more for a large application."
msgstr ""

msgid "Slight throughput reduction. This was observed at the time of writing, but ongoing JDK improvements are expected to close the gap while also allowing for achieving this max throughput sooner."
msgstr ""

msgid "Additional build step. A training run exercises the application to populate the cache. But the Quarkus infrastructure provides an automated training step based on integration tests."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This feature requires JDK 24 or newer.\n"
"Given this feature is new and evolves a lot, it is recommended to use the latest JDK."
msgstr ""

msgid "For detailed setup and configuration, see the xref:aot.adoc[AOT caching guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "jlink custom runtime image"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `jlink` extension produces a custom Java runtime image that contains only the JDK modules your application needs.\n"
"The result is a self-contained directory with its own `java` launcher, so no separate JDK installation is required on the target machine."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the extension to your project:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Then build normally:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The image is written to `target/jlink-output/image` and can be run via its `bin/` launcher script."
msgstr ""

msgid "The `jlink` extension is experimental and requires Java 25 or later."
msgstr ""

msgid "A jlink image is useful when:"
msgstr ""

msgid "You want a smaller JDK footprint without going fully native."
msgstr ""

msgid "You control the target OS and architecture and can produce an image that matches it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Experimental status. The extension and its output format may change."
msgstr ""

msgid "Platform-specific. The image runs only on the OS/architecture it was built for (unless you cross-compile)."
msgstr ""

msgid "This feature requires JDK 25 or newer."
msgstr ""

msgid "For full details, see the xref:jlink.adoc[jlink packaging guide] and the xref:modularity.adoc[modularity guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Native executable"
msgstr "ネイティブ実行可能ファイル"

msgid ""
"Quarkus applications can be compiled to native executables using GraalVM or Mandrel.\n"
"Native executables start in milliseconds, use a fraction of the memory of a JVM process, and produce the smallest possible container images."
msgstr ""

msgid "Build a native executable with:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The resulting binary is placed in the build output directory and can be run directly:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Native executables are the best choice when:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Startup time is critical: serverless / FaaS, CLI tools, or scale-to-zero environments."
msgstr ""

msgid "Memory is constrained: dense container deployments or edge devices."
msgstr ""

msgid "You want the smallest container images. Native images can be under 50 MB."
msgstr ""

msgid "Lower peak throughput. Without the JVM's JIT compiler, long-running workloads typically see lower throughput. Quarkus provides experimental support for Profile-Guided Optimization (PGO), which can help close this gap."
msgstr ""

msgid "Long build times. Native compilation typically takes 2 to 10 minutes and requires 4 to 8 GB of RAM. Powerful hardware can bring this under 2 minutes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Limited JVM tooling. Standard debuggers, profilers, and JFR are not available (though GraalVM provides alternatives)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reflection and dynamic class loading require explicit configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "For a detailed comparison of JVM, AOT, and native performance characteristics, see the xref:building-native-image.adoc#comparing-jvm-aot-native[comparison table] in the native executable guide."
msgstr ""

